                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Interviewer Responses To a Feedback Questionnaire"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1771498713626"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_INTERVIEWER_RESPONSES_TO_A_FEEDBACK_QUESTIONNAIRE_LLM",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1771500313828",
                  "id": "1771498432481",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1771498432484_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an interview feedback payload generation engine.\nAnalyze the provided interview transcript and multiple questionnaires (with questions and predefined answer options).\nYour task is to map relevant answers to each feedback question by carefully interpreting the transcript content.\nFor each questionnaire, generate a separate payload matching the following schema : {{$context.$variables.FeedbackResponsesSchema}} \n\n### Context :\nTranscript: {{$context.$variables.InterviewTranscript}}\nQuestion-Answers Mapping: {{$context.$variables.QuestionnaireQuestionsAndAnswers}} \nValidation Attributes : MaximumLength,MinimumLength,MinimumDate,MaximumDate,MinimumSelections,MaximumSelections,Mandatory\n\n### Validation Rules :\nWhen generating answers, the LLM must strictly respect the following attributes and validation rules:\nMaximumLength : The response text must not exceed the specified MaximumLength characters.\nMinimumLength : The response text must contain at least the specified MinimumLength characters.\nMinimumDate : If the answer contains a date, it must not be earlier than the specified MinimumDate\nMaximumDate : If the answer contains a date, it must not be later than the specified MaximumDate.\nMinimumSelections : For multi-select questions, the number of selected answers must be greater than or equal to MinimumSelections.\nMaximumSelections : For multi-select questions, the number of selected answers must not exceed MaximumSelections.\nMandatory : If Mandatory is Y, an answer must always be provided and cannot be null or empty.\n\n### Instructions:\n1. Transcript Analysis\n- Read the entire interview transcript carefully provided.\n- Identify statements, explanations, examples, and behaviors that directly or indirectly answer the feedback questions for each interviewer.\n\n2. QuestionÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Å“Answer Mapping\nFor each feedback question:\n- Match the most relevant AnswerId based on the transcript.\n- If multiple answers apply, select the best matches.\n- Consider the answers of the respective question. Do not consider other question answers.\n\n3. Text-Type Questions Handling\n- For questions of type TEXT / FREE_TEXT:\n- Generate a concise, relevant response derived strictly from the interview transcript.\n- Do not invent or assume information not present in the transcript.\n- Summarize or paraphrase using professional feedback language.\n\n### Output Requirements (STRICT)\n- For each question in each questionnaire and feedback request:\n- For questions with \"QuestionType\": \"1CHOICE\", set the \"QuestionAnswerId\" to the correct answerÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s ID based on transcript evidence. Set \"AnswerList\" and \"AnswerLargeObject\" to null.\n- For questions with \"QuestionType\": \"MULTCHOICE\", set the \"AnswerList\" to a comma-separated list of the matching \"AnswerId\" values whose selection is indicated by the transcript; set \"QuestionAnswerId\" and \"AnswerLargeObject\" to null.\n- For questions with \"QuestionType\": \"TEXT\", compose a summary analysis from the transcript as \"AnswerLargeObject\"; set \"QuestionAnswerId\" and \"AnswerList\" to null.\n- If \"ConditionalDisplay\" is \"Y\", only respond to this question if : ControllingQuestionId has already been answered, AND the userâ€™s selected AnswerId for that controlling question equals this questionâ€™s ControllingAnswerId. Otherwise: do not respond to it.\n- Do not include any explanations, preambles, or markdownÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬ï¿½output only a valid and complete JSON response.\n- Provide rating for the candidate from each interviewer on a scale of 1 to 5, 1 being the least and 5 being the best.\n- Always validate the response against validation rules.\n- If the generated answer violates any of the above validation rules, regenerate or adjust the response to comply with the rules.\n\n### Constraints:\n- Do not add or modify Ids.\n- Do not merge questionnaires.\n- Ensure all arrays and null values are explicitly present.\n- JSON must be syntactically valid and production-ready.\n- Ensure structural consistency for downstream processing."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Read and Parse LLM Response",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const llmResponse =  $context.$nodes.PROCESS_TRANSCRIPTS_LOOP.GENERATE_INTERVIEWER_RESPONSES_TO_A_FEEDBACK_QUESTIONNAIRE_LLM.$output;\nlet parsedResponse;\nif (typeof llmResponse === 'string') {\n parsedResponse = JSON.stringify(llmResponse);\n parsedResponse  = llmResponse.replace(/\\\\n/g,\"\");\n parsedResponse = parsedResponse.replace(/\\\\/g,\"\");\n parsedResponse = JSON.parse(parsedResponse);\n} else {\n  // Handle non-string as needed\n  parsedResponse = JSON.stringify(llmResponse);\n  parsedResponse  = parsedResponse .replace(/\\\\n/g,\"\");\n  parsedResponse = parsedResponse.replace(/\\\\/g,\"\");\n  parsedResponse= JSON.parse(parsedResponse);\n}\n\nconst parts = (parsedResponse ?.questionnaireResponses ?? []).map((qr, idx) => ({\n    payload: {\n      Status: \"I\",\n      QuestionnaireVersionNumber: String(qr.qstnrVersionNumber), // keep as string to match schema example\n      questionResponses: (qr.questionResponses ?? []).map((r) => ({\n        QuestionnaireQuestionId: String(r.QuestionnaireQuestionId),\n        QuestionAnswerId: r.QuestionAnswerId === null || r.QuestionAnswerId === undefined ? null : String(r.QuestionAnswerId),\n        AnswerList: r.AnswerList === null || r.AnswerList === undefined ? null : String(r.AnswerList) + \",\",\n        AnswerLargeObject:\n          r.AnswerLargeObject === null || r.AnswerLargeObject === undefined ? null : String(r.AnswerLargeObject),\n      })),\n    },\n    feedbackRequestId:qr.feedbackRequestId,\n    rating:qr.rating\n  }));\n\nreturn { parts };"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1771499713442"
                  },
                  "code": "READ_AND_PARSE_LLM_RESPONSE",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1771500313828",
                  "id": "1771498713626",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "type": "CODE"
                },
                {
